(7669275, 1251563, 182284, '<td valign="top">[img][/img]</td>', '[img][/img]', '2020-07-10 01:14:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669324, 1251673, 173844, '<td valign="top">I''m immediately drawn to the delicate calligraphy of these shadows, as if the leaves and stems are aching to talk to us.  How can we reach back to them?  The welter of tawny vegetation in the foreground seems to stymie the full flower of such eloquence.  Then the grainy, tonally complex wall against which this plays out bears wandering reflection, the stage, the footlights of the sun drawing out the scene.  Modest and complete, a peek into unspoken mysteries.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I''m immediately drawn to the delicate calligraphy of these shadows, as if the leaves and stems are aching to talk to us.  How can we reach back to them?  The welter of tawny vegetation in the foreground seems to stymie the full flower of such eloquence.  Then the grainy, tonally complex wall against which this plays out bears wandering reflection, the stage, the footlights of the sun drawing out the scene.  Modest and complete, a peek into unspoken mysteries.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 16:31:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669327, 1251273, 173844, '<td valign="top">Yes, the deliberate disorientation throwing us into freefall, attempting to right ourselves and so again the world.  If I may be so pretentious in making pronouncements, art often endeavors to shake us free, afford space to launch ourselves over the rutted pathways of hard set perception.  How wonderful that mere rotation can be so successful.  Another thing about your image that strikes me are the lines and patterns set up by your use of saturation.  Seems bizarre that an aspect of black and white photography, banishing color to bring out line and form, can be brought to the fore by assertive saturation creating its own establishment of emphasis.  So we''re thrust into abstraction as well as disorientation.  I really enjoy these transformations.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Yes, the deliberate disorientation throwing us into freefall, attempting to right ourselves and so again the world.  If I may be so pretentious in making pronouncements, art often endeavors to shake us free, afford space to launch ourselves over the rutted pathways of hard set perception.  How wonderful that mere rotation can be so successful.  Another thing about your image that strikes me are the lines and patterns set up by your use of saturation.  Seems bizarre that an aspect of black and white photography, banishing color to bring out line and form, can be brought to the fore by assertive saturation creating its own establishment of emphasis.  So we''re thrust into abstraction as well as disorientation.  I really enjoy these transformations.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 16:45:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669332, 1251683, 173844, '<td valign="top">Curtains are always tantalizing, as can be someone peeking out from behind a fan.  The murky frond in the background is the watcher, a subtle cross hatching endowing the image with visual and emotional depth.  So satisfying.  But there''s more!  You''ve also involved us in a beautiful study of shapely and toned lines, as they welcome the light.  I love how the composition is balanced by its opposite corners, background frond and triangle of vertical leaflets.  The sepia presentation enhances the visual revelation of black and white with breathing, organic brown.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Curtains are always tantalizing, as can be someone peeking out from behind a fan.  The murky frond in the background is the watcher, a subtle cross hatching endowing the image with visual and emotional depth.  So satisfying.  But there''s more!  You''ve also involved us in a beautiful study of shapely and toned lines, as they welcome the light.  I love how the composition is balanced by its opposite corners, background frond and triangle of vertical leaflets.  The sepia presentation enhances the visual revelation of black and white with breathing, organic brown.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 16:55:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669333, 1251316, 173844, '<td valign="top">It''s just that twist imparted by your lens, undigitizng the rectilinear scene, that moves us into a new appreciation of our world.  Slight and kind of subtle, yet powerful.  And you''ve found a section of the urban forest that''s varied in color and form.  What I find most fascinating is the framing.  It''s so unusual, curved in such a fashion, balcony and upper clouds, that we seem to be looking out of an eye.  It makes the image compellingly personal for us, psychologically involving.  It shifts our entire relationship to the photograph.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'It''s just that twist imparted by your lens, undigitizng the rectilinear scene, that moves us into a new appreciation of our world.  Slight and kind of subtle, yet powerful.  And you''ve found a section of the urban forest that''s varied in color and form.  What I find most fascinating is the framing.  It''s so unusual, curved in such a fashion, balcony and upper clouds, that we seem to be looking out of an eye.  It makes the image compellingly personal for us, psychologically involving.  It shifts our entire relationship to the photograph.  Nice title.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 17:03:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669336, 1251684, 173844, '<td valign="top">What seems, at first glance, almost a mirrored image, reveals a nuanced music upon spending time with it.  The lines of windows, roofs (or, more appealing, rooves) and corners are kind of a counterpoint to the overall scene, unprepossessing, one section of the orchestra.  The halves of the picture are like twins who have developed personal variations on a theme.  The tree on the right says, "I''m four minutes older," the building on the left is more extroverted.  Nice textures and tones on the walls, soft in the early, or late, light.  The three buildings conduct a conversation, visual and chatty.  The darker lines on the grass in the foreground strongly anchor the composition.  The sky, a beautiful purple/blue, is wonderfully encompassing.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'What seems, at first glance, almost a mirrored image, reveals a nuanced music upon spending time with it.  The lines of windows, roofs (or, more appealing, rooves) and corners are kind of a counterpoint to the overall scene, unprepossessing, one section of the orchestra.  The halves of the picture are like twins who have developed personal variations on a theme.  The tree on the right says, "I''m four minutes older," the building on the left is more extroverted.  Nice textures and tones on the walls, soft in the early, or late, light.  The three buildings conduct a conversation, visual and chatty.  The darker lines on the grass in the foreground strongly anchor the composition.  The sky, a beautiful purple/blue, is wonderfully encompassing.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 17:22:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669337, 1251723, 173844, '<td valign="top">Funny how you sometimes turn the key, open the door, and you''re inside a Tardis (Dr. Who reference), the new emormity a jolting surprise.  My first impression here was of a skull somewhat arbitrarily placed as a display on a rock.  Um, okay.  Then, in a mind-bending optical shift, it becomes a fish, head left, smiling, holding still just above the ocean floor.  From macabre to glee, a magical, fascinating toggle.  Bravissimo!<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Funny how you sometimes turn the key, open the door, and you''re inside a Tardis (Dr. Who reference), the new emormity a jolting surprise.  My first impression here was of a skull somewhat arbitrarily placed as a display on a rock.  Um, okay.  Then, in a mind-bending optical shift, it becomes a fish, head left, smiling, holding still just above the ocean floor.  From macabre to glee, a magical, fascinating toggle.  Bravissimo!Thank you.', '2020-07-10 17:39:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669340, 1251681, 173844, '<td valign="top">I''m a big fan of rust, how it eats away at practical perfection, how it reveals the beautiful potential hidden deep within iron''s genome.  Insidiously partnered with oxygen.  If, as here, it''s orange being flaked away, a happy tone poem arises.  Of course if the shapes are artfully presented in a dyamic composition, now you''ve got something.  I like the recession of planes born of the softening focus.  The dark flats nicely set off the orange.  There''s even a sense of green or blue in them.  Your perspective adds a monumental dimension.  A strong statement.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I''m a big fan of rust, how it eats away at practical perfection, how it reveals the beautiful potential hidden deep within iron''s genome.  Insidiously partnered with oxygen.  If, as here, it''s orange being flaked away, a happy tone poem arises.  Of course if the shapes are artfully presented in a dyamic composition, now you''ve got something.  I like the recession of planes born of the softening focus.  The dark flats nicely set off the orange.  There''s even a sense of green or blue in them.  Your perspective adds a monumental dimension.  A strong statement.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 17:47:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669358, 1251662, 173844, '<td valign="top">A straight up and very pleasing design, where the lines echo each other, both thin and wide.  Flute and bassoon?  The dark triangles of the openings are more percussive.  Neither simple nor overbusy, I''d call it friendly.  The way you''ve marched the vertical line along diagonally gives the image its dynamic energy.  Recedes nicely to complex abstraction.  Perfect in black and white.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'A straight up and very pleasing design, where the lines echo each other, both thin and wide.  Flute and bassoon?  The dark triangles of the openings are more percussive.  Neither simple nor overbusy, I''d call it friendly.  The way you''ve marched the vertical line along diagonally gives the image its dynamic energy.  Recedes nicely to complex abstraction.  Perfect in black and white.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 19:37:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669361, 1251340, 173844, '<td valign="top">A straightforward, ordinary moment excellently done.  It''s stripped of pretension and striving, honors this instant of time and I think promises the next and the next.  The man is of a piece, creased with age, labor and sun, from feet to head.  It helps that the light picks out his character and throws shadows at angles.  Even the traffic works in harmony.  Reminds me of Robert Frank without the drapery of symbolism.  I only wish I had the ability to take a picture like this.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'A straightforward, ordinary moment excellently done.  It''s stripped of pretension and striving, honors this instant of time and I think promises the next and the next.  The man is of a piece, creased with age, labor and sun, from feet to head.  It helps that the light picks out his character and throws shadows at angles.  Even the traffic works in harmony.  Reminds me of Robert Frank without the drapery of symbolism.  I only wish I had the ability to take a picture like this.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 20:04:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669364, 1251560, 173844, '<td valign="top">What an appealing portrailt of a sweet dog!  What so much appeals to me here are the pose, the pale fabric upon which he or she lies and the cropping.  They''re all unusual enough to invite us in, and now our attention is riveted by her/his face, eyes, the trusting approach of the pose.  It has a high key feel even though there''s plenty of dark in the fur.  It''s a very interestilng presentation, and all in all you''re fortunate to have such a beautiful/handsome companion.  And I wonder if your title is a play on Mochi, my dog''s name.  Also a moocher.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'What an appealing portrailt of a sweet dog!  What so much appeals to me here are the pose, the pale fabric upon which he or she lies and the cropping.  They''re all unusual enough to invite us in, and now our attention is riveted by her/his face, eyes, the trusting approach of the pose.  It has a high key feel even though there''s plenty of dark in the fur.  It''s a very interestilng presentation, and all in all you''re fortunate to have such a beautiful/handsome companion.  And I wonder if your title is a play on Mochi, my dog''s name.  Also a moocher.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 21:28:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669365, 1251716, 173844, '<td valign="top">This is really cool, a sterling take on the usual shaking off dog picture.  The droplets spiral off this bird (tern?) in proof of aerodynamic mastery.  Catching amimals living their lives is so much more rewarding than mere illustration, not that there can''t be wonder in that, too.  But it''s the individuality that comes out, the kinship of us all.  You allow us to imagine, to feel what it is to soar along, lifted by air and propulsion, performing everyday miracles.  The darker portion of the background nicely sets off the brightnbess of the bird.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'This is really cool, a sterling take on the usual shaking off dog picture.  The droplets spiral off this bird (tern?) in proof of aerodynamic mastery.  Catching amimals living their lives is so much more rewarding than mere illustration, not that there can''t be wonder in that, too.  But it''s the individuality that comes out, the kinship of us all.  You allow us to imagine, to feel what it is to soar along, lifted by air and propulsion, performing everyday miracles.  The darker portion of the background nicely sets off the brightnbess of the bird.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 21:36:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669366, 1251464, 173844, '<td valign="top">Centered subjects need heft to pull off flouting photographic gospel.  I feel your image succeeds because this vulture is iconically stylized, forceful and confident.  It has an almost Egyptian majesty, coolly appraising the parade, knowing that we all eventually rerturn to him, or her.  That see through nasal cavity is a tiny jewel, set as it is with the sky.  The dead branch perch is perfect.  Fine command of negative space.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Centered subjects need heft to pull off flouting photographic gospel.  I feel your image succeeds because this vulture is iconically stylized, forceful and confident.  It has an almost Egyptian majesty, coolly appraising the parade, knowing that we all eventually rerturn to him, or her.  That see through nasal cavity is a tiny jewel, set as it is with the sky.  The dead branch perch is perfect.  Fine command of negative space.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 21:43:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669367, 1251691, 173844, '<td valign="top">Gonna take it on faith that these are, in fact, birdwatchers.  I like this technique of abstraction that makes terrestrial star trails, especially the sparser wisps atop it all.  After some consideration the image resolved itself into lips with three jagged teeth.  Now I was fascinated.  This goes to show that food for the imagination can be nutritious.  There''s a satisfaction in coming to terms with a mystery, yet a good case can also be made for lettilng it remain as such.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Gonna take it on faith that these are, in fact, birdwatchers.  I like this technique of abstraction that makes terrestrial star trails, especially the sparser wisps atop it all.  After some consideration the image resolved itself into lips with three jagged teeth.  Now I was fascinated.  This goes to show that food for the imagination can be nutritious.  There''s a satisfaction in coming to terms with a mystery, yet a good case can also be made for lettilng it remain as such.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 21:50:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669368, 1251665, 173844, '<td valign="top">Is this on the east side of Whimsy?  Please tell me there are North, South and West Whimsys as well.  This is a photo of tantalization.  You''ve set us up to yearn for entry into this two dimensional world, introducing tension into what should be a placid locale.  I like being playfully torn between desire and the inability to partake.  Notice "playfully."  The figures in the window seem to beckon us within.  It''s adroitly framed on the right with the advent of a now, by comparison, boring world.  The black and white presentation is interesting because it feels like the building and its surrounds are, subsequently, emotionally in color. <br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Is this on the east side of Whimsy?  Please tell me there are North, South and West Whimsys as well.  This is a photo of tantalization.  You''ve set us up to yearn for entry into this two dimensional world, introducing tension into what should be a placid locale.  I like being playfully torn between desire and the inability to partake.  Notice "playfully."  The figures in the window seem to beckon us within.  It''s adroitly framed on the right with the advent of a now, by comparison, boring world.  The black and white presentation is interesting because it feels like the building and its surrounds are, subsequently, emotionally in color. Thank you.', '2020-07-10 22:01:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669371, 1251719, 173844, '<td valign="top">Interesting image that''s hard to focus on realistically and therefore transforms itself into abstraction.  It''s busy, even dizzying, with frantic lines, shapes and textures rising like a tidal wave.  I find I can settle it down by softening my vision and seeing it as a force field.  It''s an unusual sensation that induces a sense of being both energized and exhausted.  It''s op art wrought of everyday objects, and quite creative.  My wife, who taught math, just wandered by and said, "Oh, I like that.  It''s very mathematical."  Also, to appreciate the title, it does seem like the game of go.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Interesting image that''s hard to focus on realistically and therefore transforms itself into abstraction.  It''s busy, even dizzying, with frantic lines, shapes and textures rising like a tidal wave.  I find I can settle it down by softening my vision and seeing it as a force field.  It''s an unusual sensation that induces a sense of being both energized and exhausted.  It''s op art wrought of everyday objects, and quite creative.  My wife, who taught math, just wandered by and said, "Oh, I like that.  It''s very mathematical."  Also, to appreciate the title, it does seem like the game of go.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 22:23:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669372, 1251679, 173844, '<td valign="top">Very interesting study of shape, line, texture, color, contrast and composition.  It all comes together quite naturally.  Although you can tease apart the constituent elements, they make little sense until they''re restored to their harmonious balance.  I like the colors and the play of dark and light.  The more I look at it the more I appreciate it.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Very interesting study of shape, line, texture, color, contrast and composition.  It all comes together quite naturally.  Although you can tease apart the constituent elements, they make little sense until they''re restored to their harmonious balance.  I like the colors and the play of dark and light.  The more I look at it the more I appreciate it.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 22:28:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669373, 1251563, 173844, '<td valign="top">A corner of the barn, way in the back, now in the harsh light seems caught in flagrante delicto.  It would be ingenuous not to say so.  It also raises all sorts of psychological and philosophical questions.  It''s for the good and elevates the image.  I hope I''m not hijacking your photograph on a rocket to fantasy-land.  If so, I apologize.  It certainly stands as a study of line, texture and tone.  But I can''t help seeing a commentary on gender travail and intimations of potential violence.  Pitchforks plunge into hay.  I''m taking it as a superior allegory.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'A corner of the barn, way in the back, now in the harsh light seems caught in flagrante delicto.  It would be ingenuous not to say so.  It also raises all sorts of psychological and philosophical questions.  It''s for the good and elevates the image.  I hope I''m not hijacking your photograph on a rocket to fantasy-land.  If so, I apologize.  It certainly stands as a study of line, texture and tone.  But I can''t help seeing a commentary on gender travail and intimations of potential violence.  Pitchforks plunge into hay.  I''m taking it as a superior allegory.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 22:36:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669374, 1251443, 173844, '<td valign="top">I certainly have to grin, loving dogs and their ways.  You have a sweet sense of humor.  The point of focus, so rightly on her or his expression, leaves the remainder of a meal, close to us, in soft focus.  This generalizes the object of desire and brings out a universal truth about dogs and food.  My first thought was, "I''m going to get there first," but I''ve been beaten out so many times by my dog that this might be a pipe dream.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I certainly have to grin, loving dogs and their ways.  You have a sweet sense of humor.  The point of focus, so rightly on her or his expression, leaves the remainder of a meal, close to us, in soft focus.  This generalizes the object of desire and brings out a universal truth about dogs and food.  My first thought was, "I''m going to get there first," but I''ve been beaten out so many times by my dog that this might be a pipe dream.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 22:43:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669375, 1251661, 173844, '<td valign="top">Fallen trees are one thing, part of the natural cycle, stumps are another.  All to often, but far from always, they feel like just the termination of noble life for profit and convenience.  My stated position certainly clashes with my training and partial career as a cabinetmaker.  How often I was caught up short while working with oak, say, remembering this was once a living tree.  So much for my high horse.  In any case, this is a poignant image of a ghost in the bright sunshine, coddled by upcoming gererations.  It''s an object of beauty, streamlined and mysterious.  I like how you''ve made a portrait of it.  Grays and green go well together,  Nevertheless, stumps are trees'' own tombstones.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Fallen trees are one thing, part of the natural cycle, stumps are another.  All to often, but far from always, they feel like just the termination of noble life for profit and convenience.  My stated position certainly clashes with my training and partial career as a cabinetmaker.  How often I was caught up short while working with oak, say, remembering this was once a living tree.  So much for my high horse.  In any case, this is a poignant image of a ghost in the bright sunshine, coddled by upcoming gererations.  It''s an object of beauty, streamlined and mysterious.  I like how you''ve made a portrait of it.  Grays and green go well together,  Nevertheless, stumps are trees'' own tombstones.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 22:51:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669376, 1251712, 173844, '<td valign="top">I like how you''ve provided both image and commentary.  The buildings, and the perspective you''ve established, offer a Mondrian-esque scene.  The shapes, like a puzzle being solved, and the bright colors delight the eye.  It''s also neat how the shadows and reflections are reminders of a surrounding context.  The signs on the fence anchor and inform the photograph.  Their cautionary, warning nature serve dual purposes.  Stay away from the site as it''s dangerous.  Also, stay away from art, likewise dangerous and problematic.  A nice, slippery conjunction.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I like how you''ve provided both image and commentary.  The buildings, and the perspective you''ve established, offer a Mondrian-esque scene.  The shapes, like a puzzle being solved, and the bright colors delight the eye.  It''s also neat how the shadows and reflections are reminders of a surrounding context.  The signs on the fence anchor and inform the photograph.  Their cautionary, warning nature serve dual purposes.  Stay away from the site as it''s dangerous.  Also, stay away from art, likewise dangerous and problematic.  A nice, slippery conjunction.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 23:09:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669377, 1251320, 173844, '<td valign="top">This is a short poem, fine for reflection, peaceful and subtle.  It''s a ballet of shapes, yet without leaps and pirouettes.  Hexagonal flagstones and varied rectangles just as they are, a wordless reminder of the simple pleasure of form.  I like your composition, and the fretwork of cement that unobtrusively provides strength to the whole, making it possible.  Like the bottom people in a human pyramid.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'This is a short poem, fine for reflection, peaceful and subtle.  It''s a ballet of shapes, yet without leaps and pirouettes.  Hexagonal flagstones and varied rectangles just as they are, a wordless reminder of the simple pleasure of form.  I like your composition, and the fretwork of cement that unobtrusively provides strength to the whole, making it possible.  Like the bottom people in a human pyramid.Thank you.', '2020-07-10 23:14:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669381, 1251724, 100831, '<td valign="top">Excellent. King of the hill. Love those lines and the grays are perfect, just the right contrast.</td>', 'Excellent. King of the hill. Love those lines and the grays are perfect, just the right contrast.', '2020-07-11 00:33:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669382, 1251617, 173844, '<td valign="top">I like your use of brickwork to provide a white background.  The texture and subtle toning participate in the image.  I also like the spiky jitter of rosemary, its lines projecting every which way off a strong vertical.  This balanced by the underemphasized horizontals of the layers of cement. Key is the bright sunlight that brings out the rosemary, and causses it to fade into the background lower down.  Thus it seems evanescent, a shimmer of shyness.  A wallflower?<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I like your use of brickwork to provide a white background.  The texture and subtle toning participate in the image.  I also like the spiky jitter of rosemary, its lines projecting every which way off a strong vertical.  This balanced by the underemphasized horizontals of the layers of cement. Key is the bright sunlight that brings out the rosemary, and causses it to fade into the background lower down.  Thus it seems evanescent, a shimmer of shyness.  A wallflower?Thank you.', '2020-07-11 00:34:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669383, 1251712, 100831, '<td valign="top">The signs win.  I think this is great, especially the reflection in the window and the similar shadow below. Good Color.</td>', 'The signs win.  I think this is great, especially the reflection in the window and the similar shadow below. Good Color.', '2020-07-11 00:36:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669384, 1251407, 100831, '<td valign="top">Indeed!</td>', 'Indeed!', '2020-07-11 00:37:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669385, 1251673, 100831, '<td valign="top">The light of my life.</td>', 'The light of my life.', '2020-07-11 00:38:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669387, 1251541, 173844, '<td valign="top">What jumps out first are the smiles, the sense of playfulness and ease.  I don''t make out, though it''s possible, undertones of hostility.  As we in America come to an increased focus on the terrible consequences of a history of violence, oppression, fear and unkindness, I hope I correctly see this sparring as one more incident of normal, human interaction.  The gentleman on the left seems to beckon us in.  I''m not a pollyanna, though, and see this movement as a positive step on a long trek.  Amidst all the visual clamor the bright white reflective stripes on the workmen''s vests serve to establish a motif that introduces some order and a place for the eyes to rest.  Black and white treatment also allows the background to resolve into a complex melange of shapes.  Nicely seen.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'What jumps out first are the smiles, the sense of playfulness and ease.  I don''t make out, though it''s possible, undertones of hostility.  As we in America come to an increased focus on the terrible consequences of a history of violence, oppression, fear and unkindness, I hope I correctly see this sparring as one more incident of normal, human interaction.  The gentleman on the left seems to beckon us in.  I''m not a pollyanna, though, and see this movement as a positive step on a long trek.  Amidst all the visual clamor the bright white reflective stripes on the workmen''s vests serve to establish a motif that introduces some order and a place for the eyes to rest.  Black and white treatment also allows the background to resolve into a complex melange of shapes.  Nicely seen.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 00:46:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669403, 1251627, 173844, '<td valign="top">Good form!  She or he is striking looking with those orange eyes and golden halos about them.  Perfect focus on his/her face.  In the summer heat it''s actually cooling to imagine the pleasure s/he feels.  (This he/she, etc., is really cumbersome.  Couldn''t animals, pets at least, distinguish their gender in an obvious way?  Hats, for example.  Pink and blue, stripes and solids, panama and fez, and so on.  Who''s with me?)  Additionally, I like how the sand in the shallows can be seen as tan lines and patches due to the angles of sun, waves and you.  Glimpses of another kingdom.  This is the kind of picture one treasures.  My dog at play.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Good form!  She or he is striking looking with those orange eyes and golden halos about them.  Perfect focus on his/her face.  In the summer heat it''s actually cooling to imagine the pleasure s/he feels.  (This he/she, etc., is really cumbersome.  Couldn''t animals, pets at least, distinguish their gender in an obvious way?  Hats, for example.  Pink and blue, stripes and solids, panama and fez, and so on.  Who''s with me?)  Additionally, I like how the sand in the shallows can be seen as tan lines and patches due to the angles of sun, waves and you.  Glimpses of another kingdom.  This is the kind of picture one treasures.  My dog at play.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 10:46:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669404, 1251503, 173844, '<td valign="top">To me, this image is about the rope.  It can toll the bell, glad tidings or mourning, to mark time or to call people in.  But it can also be a truss, a noose (tempted to let my typo, "moose", stand.), an instrument of captivity. I view it warily.  The colorful flowers beneath the bell are like grace notes, visual echoes.  The bell itself is such an interesting shape, amply capable of its central role.  The tight focus on the bell and wooden structure affords a peek into the world beyond, which seems a bit magical.  A melange of sight and sound.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'To me, this image is about the rope.  It can toll the bell, glad tidings or mourning, to mark time or to call people in.  But it can also be a truss, a noose (tempted to let my typo, "moose", stand.), an instrument of captivity. I view it warily.  The colorful flowers beneath the bell are like grace notes, visual echoes.  The bell itself is such an interesting shape, amply capable of its central role.  The tight focus on the bell and wooden structure affords a peek into the world beyond, which seems a bit magical.  A melange of sight and sound.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 10:59:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669405, 1251594, 173844, '<td valign="top">Is that state of mind unbalanced or dynamically balanced?  You leave that up to the viewer to settle.  What I settled upon is that the poles are peering downward, like three wise men.  To draw away from orthodoxy, I choose to see this scene as veneration of nature, its profuse beauty.  The foreground leaves shine with light.  It''s, for me, a difficult image to understand, but that''s how it goes sometimes, and often for the better.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Is that state of mind unbalanced or dynamically balanced?  You leave that up to the viewer to settle.  What I settled upon is that the poles are peering downward, like three wise men.  To draw away from orthodoxy, I choose to see this scene as veneration of nature, its profuse beauty.  The foreground leaves shine with light.  It''s, for me, a difficult image to understand, but that''s how it goes sometimes, and often for the better.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 11:07:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669406, 1251721, 173844, '<td valign="top">Either this pooch has great balance or we''re looking out from the deck of a ship in turbulent waters.  In any case it''s an interesting crop, leaving Grendel kind of looking like a seal, to extend the whimsy.  Remaking an image on a slant is instant dynamism.  Grendel now seems sporty, alert and ready to explore a transformed world.  Or dive for fish.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Either this pooch has great balance or we''re looking out from the deck of a ship in turbulent waters.  In any case it''s an interesting crop, leaving Grendel kind of looking like a seal, to extend the whimsy.  Remaking an image on a slant is instant dynamism.  Grendel now seems sporty, alert and ready to explore a transformed world.  Or dive for fish.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 11:12:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669407, 1251248, 173844, '<td valign="top">A street scene with a surprise appearance by Fred Flintstone!  Oh wait, it''s a construction vehicle trying to pass as traffic, which is worthy of a double-take.  And the driver is taking it side saddle, a la Lady Godiva.  This all jumps up the moment, kicks it into a strangeness that''s abetted by a lovely toned sky, a beautiful sky.  That''s what secures the image for me.  I also like the out of focus ambiguity of the left hand framing.  Makes one wonder, curious and unsure.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'A street scene with a surprise appearance by Fred Flintstone!  Oh wait, it''s a construction vehicle trying to pass as traffic, which is worthy of a double-take.  And the driver is taking it side saddle, a la Lady Godiva.  This all jumps up the moment, kicks it into a strangeness that''s abetted by a lovely toned sky, a beautiful sky.  That''s what secures the image for me.  I also like the out of focus ambiguity of the left hand framing.  Makes one wonder, curious and unsure.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 11:18:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669408, 1251202, 173844, '<td valign="top">A lovely cascade of mauve-ish shadows, a temporay signature of the sun.  I love those decorative curlicues on handrails.  The world ia a multi-faceted sun dial, and here''s the time and news of the day, if only we can decipher it.  The horizontal lines of the steps and doorway set up a staff for these besotted notes.  The delicate washes of color are also very appealing.  I think I''d appreciate the image more without the plant, which tends to draw the eye away from an otherwise tender emptiness.  But that''s just a subjective take, and can''t detract from an image that speaks to me.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'A lovely cascade of mauve-ish shadows, a temporay signature of the sun.  I love those decorative curlicues on handrails.  The world ia a multi-faceted sun dial, and here''s the time and news of the day, if only we can decipher it.  The horizontal lines of the steps and doorway set up a staff for these besotted notes.  The delicate washes of color are also very appealing.  I think I''d appreciate the image more without the plant, which tends to draw the eye away from an otherwise tender emptiness.  But that''s just a subjective take, and can''t detract from an image that speaks to me.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 11:27:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669409, 1251715, 173844, '<td valign="top">A dreamy confection, assuredly beautiful.  The softness of the moonlight and trees stirs up longing and, yes, faith.  So much given through this hint of eternity.  I''m sorry, further commentary would just muddy the sublime.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'A dreamy confection, assuredly beautiful.  The softness of the moonlight and trees stirs up longing and, yes, faith.  So much given through this hint of eternity.  I''m sorry, further commentary would just muddy the sublime.  Nice title.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 11:31:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669411, 1251585, 173844, '<td valign="top">Ah, thanks for the nod to my name, as they hang out doing what they do, coo and court, ever on the lookout for tidbits.  With or without them, this is a splendid image.  I love how the end of the dimly lit street flares out into a fanfare of bright sunlight.  It hangs a sheer curtain of haze before the looming mountain across the way.  Sweet how that both keeps attention on the foreground neighborhood and offhandedly beckons us afield.  The walls close in but don''t, at least during daytime, feel claustrophobic.  This because of how it opens up.  I especially like the street lanterns.  They seem to encompass the atmosphere within, a chiming harmony with the day.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Ah, thanks for the nod to my name, as they hang out doing what they do, coo and court, ever on the lookout for tidbits.  With or without them, this is a splendid image.  I love how the end of the dimly lit street flares out into a fanfare of bright sunlight.  It hangs a sheer curtain of haze before the looming mountain across the way.  Sweet how that both keeps attention on the foreground neighborhood and offhandedly beckons us afield.  The walls close in but don''t, at least during daytime, feel claustrophobic.  This because of how it opens up.  I especially like the street lanterns.  They seem to encompass the atmosphere within, a chiming harmony with the day.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 11:49:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669412, 1251650, 173844, '<td valign="top">Wow, what you''ve found and how you present this striking image are jaw-dropping.  I guess this is a vehicle of some sort, but transformed by the heady alchemy of stripes hugging its contours.  Moire on psychedelics.  Quite plenty so far, but then it appears to be a face of some bizarre sort.  As such it''s implacably opaque, an alien being.  I hardly know what to make ot besides that it''s stunning.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Wow, what you''ve found and how you present this striking image are jaw-dropping.  I guess this is a vehicle of some sort, but transformed by the heady alchemy of stripes hugging its contours.  Moire on psychedelics.  Quite plenty so far, but then it appears to be a face of some bizarre sort.  As such it''s implacably opaque, an alien being.  I hardly know what to make ot besides that it''s stunning.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 11:54:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669414, 1251675, 173844, '<td valign="top">Usually I look askance at photos that trade on other people''s artwork, but this fine image is made of the framing.  The central (delightful) art is in service of irony, contrast, commentary, and whatever more that I don''t fathom.  I''m thinking this is about absence, loneliness, the usurpation of joy by isolation.  Or not.  The central picture might be a window on yesterdays, figurative childhood.  It''s haunting and poignant.  The composition of free-form grid is tempered by a fleeting view of this man''s head, the picture and the clock.  Lots of pleasing grays, especially the thrown spectrum on the upper left.  Moving minimalism.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Usually I look askance at photos that trade on other people''s artwork, but this fine image is made of the framing.  The central (delightful) art is in service of irony, contrast, commentary, and whatever more that I don''t fathom.  I''m thinking this is about absence, loneliness, the usurpation of joy by isolation.  Or not.  The central picture might be a window on yesterdays, figurative childhood.  It''s haunting and poignant.  The composition of free-form grid is tempered by a fleeting view of this man''s head, the picture and the clock.  Lots of pleasing grays, especially the thrown spectrum on the upper left.  Moving minimalism.  Nice title.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 12:15:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669425, 1251541, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like how the "battle" of the two workers on the right is reflected by a "battle" between the worker on the left and the viewer. And in spite of all this war everyone has a happy expression. A refreshingly playful scene.</td>', 'I like how the "battle" of the two workers on the right is reflected by a "battle" between the worker on the left and the viewer. And in spite of all this war everyone has a happy expression. A refreshingly playful scene.', '2020-07-11 15:13:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669427, 1251722, 50695, '<td valign="top">so much geometry. Duchamp might have made this. what a gorgeous shadow.</td>', 'so much geometry. Duchamp might have made this. what a gorgeous shadow.', '2020-07-11 15:15:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669428, 1251248, 50695, '<td valign="top">a messy shot, like so much of our experience. no time to compose things properly. no time to separate the colors from the whites. just a glimpse of a moment.</td>', 'a messy shot, like so much of our experience. no time to compose things properly. no time to separate the colors from the whites. just a glimpse of a moment.', '2020-07-11 15:17:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669429, 1251681, 50695, '<td valign="top">it''s all about the right amount of complexity. Not enough and it''s dull, too much and it''s confusing. This has a lot of angles but just a few bold shapes. This has a lot of texture but just one color. The contrast is high but the shadows are few, and they are the same color as the light areas. It''s a good abstract.</td>', 'it''s all about the right amount of complexity. Not enough and it''s dull, too much and it''s confusing. This has a lot of angles but just a few bold shapes. This has a lot of texture but just one color. The contrast is high but the shadows are few, and they are the same color as the light areas. It''s a good abstract.', '2020-07-11 15:20:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669430, 1251704, 50695, '<td valign="top">how little we think of the consequences of our actions, the marks we leave behind, but one day that is all that will be left of us. And look, we''re almost gone already.</td>', 'how little we think of the consequences of our actions, the marks we leave behind, but one day that is all that will be left of us. And look, we''re almost gone already.', '2020-07-11 15:21:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669431, 1251661, 50695, '<td valign="top">five ghosts possess a tree stump, contented to sit still and look out at the world they''ve left behind.</td>', 'five ghosts possess a tree stump, contented to sit still and look out at the world they''ve left behind.', '2020-07-11 15:22:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669433, 1251708, 173844, '<td valign="top">There are so many places this could be, but I''m fixing it at what I know, Central Park in NYC.  Pardon me if I''m wrong.  In any case, I''ve often tried to make something of these somber, elegnt tunnels, to no avail.  I didn''t have the magic ingredient - children, and dancing within the overspilling light.  The leading lines of perspective are subtle.  The lit up electrical conduit pipe coming from the upper left, and the lights, which I''d probably avoid, serve to relieve and punctuate the shadowy interior.  At the far end ot the tunnel, were blown highlights ever more appropriate?  A  revelation for me.  <br/>Thank you.</td>', 'There are so many places this could be, but I''m fixing it at what I know, Central Park in NYC.  Pardon me if I''m wrong.  In any case, I''ve often tried to make something of these somber, elegnt tunnels, to no avail.  I didn''t have the magic ingredient - children, and dancing within the overspilling light.  The leading lines of perspective are subtle.  The lit up electrical conduit pipe coming from the upper left, and the lights, which I''d probably avoid, serve to relieve and punctuate the shadowy interior.  At the far end ot the tunnel, were blown highlights ever more appropriate?  A  revelation for me.  Thank you.', '2020-07-11 15:48:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669434, 1251594, 100831, '<td valign="top">Clear as a tack. Love the light and the little caps on their heads, the wise men.</td>', 'Clear as a tack. Love the light and the little caps on their heads, the wise men.', '2020-07-11 15:52:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669435, 1251560, 100831, '<td valign="top">great angle.</td>', 'great angle.', '2020-07-11 15:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669436, 1251704, 173844, '<td valign="top">I really enjoy images that are more glancing hint than statement.  Here we have to work out what''s going on, even play detective.  It took awhile to see the person and dog in the distance walking up the stairs.  Understated and evanescent.  It''s a compact, dynamic composition.  The shadows are like red herrings messing with our perception, abetting confusion and misdirection.  What tickles me most is that in addition to spacial depth, which is aparent, is depth in time.  From the paw prints to the walkers is a fullness, a span of time made palpable.  Now the image comes alive, breathing.  A marvelous and satisfying achievement.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I really enjoy images that are more glancing hint than statement.  Here we have to work out what''s going on, even play detective.  It took awhile to see the person and dog in the distance walking up the stairs.  Understated and evanescent.  It''s a compact, dynamic composition.  The shadows are like red herrings messing with our perception, abetting confusion and misdirection.  What tickles me most is that in addition to spacial depth, which is aparent, is depth in time.  From the paw prints to the walkers is a fullness, a span of time made palpable.  Now the image comes alive, breathing.  A marvelous and satisfying achievement.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 15:59:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669437, 1251407, 173844, '<td valign="top">Against all experiential and scientific dogma, it does seem that reflections sometimes do break away from what they purport to reflect.  Rebirth, do-si-do, change partners.  This image is a compelling example of just such a casual shift.  How I love how the water grasses flourish beneath the tree.  And the jittery staircase, lower right.  What fun!  Mostly I adore how whatever''s floating on the surface seems like static on an old black and white tv set.  Rod Serling approves.  Here we go, screw the commercials.  "It''s been a wonderful visit, now beam me up.  I''m not kidding, beam me up....."<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Against all experiential and scientific dogma, it does seem that reflections sometimes do break away from what they purport to reflect.  Rebirth, do-si-do, change partners.  This image is a compelling example of just such a casual shift.  How I love how the water grasses flourish beneath the tree.  And the jittery staircase, lower right.  What fun!  Mostly I adore how whatever''s floating on the surface seems like static on an old black and white tv set.  Rod Serling approves.  Here we go, screw the commercials.  "It''s been a wonderful visit, now beam me up.  I''m not kidding, beam me up....."Thank you.', '2020-07-11 16:08:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669439, 1251687, 173844, '<td valign="top">I''ve been looking lately to photograph dead flowers, summer being what it is.  This flower - rose, I''m assuming - is a gorgeous revelation.  In partial shadow, guarded by  a thorny branch, it has found a quiet corner to pass in peace.  So do some animals when they sense their time has come.  It''s what I would want.  Here''s the process. There''s the still-beating heart, muted red to pink.  It''s the resplendent, glowing brown that I linger upon.  So rich and warm.  It''s as if this flower has reflowered, a spark of karma, a second spring.  Nice composition.  The light seems aspirational.  Imparts refreshment and serenity.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I''ve been looking lately to photograph dead flowers, summer being what it is.  This flower - rose, I''m assuming - is a gorgeous revelation.  In partial shadow, guarded by  a thorny branch, it has found a quiet corner to pass in peace.  So do some animals when they sense their time has come.  It''s what I would want.  Here''s the process. There''s the still-beating heart, muted red to pink.  It''s the resplendent, glowing brown that I linger upon.  So rich and warm.  It''s as if this flower has reflowered, a spark of karma, a second spring.  Nice composition.  The light seems aspirational.  Imparts refreshment and serenity.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 16:19:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669440, 1251722, 173844, '<td valign="top">I so much enjoy this type of photo, flat on, too ordinary for those who don''t see beauty everywhere.  Please, I''m not crowning myself, it''s just a talent I admire.  Yes, its reduction to abstraction works well, its lines and interuptions, but it''s the simple beingness that endows the image with force.  The great thing is that it''s right here now, and I see you know that.  The meaning of the title isn''t apparent to me, but I''m certain it''s worthy.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'I so much enjoy this type of photo, flat on, too ordinary for those who don''t see beauty everywhere.  Please, I''m not crowning myself, it''s just a talent I admire.  Yes, its reduction to abstraction works well, its lines and interuptions, but it''s the simple beingness that endows the image with force.  The great thing is that it''s right here now, and I see you know that.  The meaning of the title isn''t apparent to me, but I''m certain it''s worthy.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 16:26:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669441, 1251724, 173844, '<td valign="top">Fine imaginative leap to see this design as a pediment.  I looked up "pedimentary" and Google insisted on sedimentary; but there is a company that offers pedimentary doors, in case anyone''s in the market.  This is wonderful, so clean and compelling, a crisp outline that thrives on negative space.  The bird adds immeasurably in completing the image, a living finial that animates the whole.  Even the gray sky shines.  The wood siding is sumptuous, each slat an individual swatch of texture and tone.  Perfect in black and white.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Fine imaginative leap to see this design as a pediment.  I looked up "pedimentary" and Google insisted on sedimentary; but there is a company that offers pedimentary doors, in case anyone''s in the market.  This is wonderful, so clean and compelling, a crisp outline that thrives on negative space.  The bird adds immeasurably in completing the image, a living finial that animates the whole.  Even the gray sky shines.  The wood siding is sumptuous, each slat an individual swatch of texture and tone.  Perfect in black and white.  Nice title.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 16:41:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669442, 1251647, 100831, '<td valign="top">Apt for the challenge, certainly... a day in the life.</td>', 'Apt for the challenge, certainly... a day in the life.', '2020-07-11 16:50:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669443, 1251254, 173844, '<td valign="top">An entrancing, fun, distinctive image that brings on a smile.  A constellation in the far reaches of the universe, brought to life, happy and welcoming.  As a child would have it.  Quirky and works so very well, and I''m grateful for it.  The composition, the colors, the vignette are all adroit.  I''d put this on my wall to keep me honest.  And what''s aglow behind that door?<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'An entrancing, fun, distinctive image that brings on a smile.  A constellation in the far reaches of the universe, brought to life, happy and welcoming.  As a child would have it.  Quirky and works so very well, and I''m grateful for it.  The composition, the colors, the vignette are all adroit.  I''d put this on my wall to keep me honest.  And what''s aglow behind that door?Thank you.', '2020-07-11 17:02:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669444, 1251622, 173844, '<td valign="top">Some images that have so much potential to be boring nevertheless offer a sparkle and tone that launches them into a higher orbit.  Here''s one.  I like the lean of these women, their anticipation, their peering into the future.  And so ably placed by the edge, focusing outward.  Their colorful outfits and bag are gently, mostly, echoed on the street and bus stop.  They''re crucial to the scene, but I also feel that they''re props for this beautiful day, lit with expectation and timelessness.  It''s in the sky trees and brick wall, a kind of emotional alpenglow.  Even if it''s processing that imparts this sensation, it gladdens the heart.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you</td>', 'Some images that have so much potential to be boring nevertheless offer a sparkle and tone that launches them into a higher orbit.  Here''s one.  I like the lean of these women, their anticipation, their peering into the future.  And so ably placed by the edge, focusing outward.  Their colorful outfits and bag are gently, mostly, echoed on the street and bus stop.  They''re crucial to the scene, but I also feel that they''re props for this beautiful day, lit with expectation and timelessness.  It''s in the sky trees and brick wall, a kind of emotional alpenglow.  Even if it''s processing that imparts this sensation, it gladdens the heart.  Nice title.Thank you', '2020-07-11 17:12:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669446, 1251647, 173844, '<td valign="top">Here it''s not enough to see and feel the image, we also have to read and think it through.  The irony of contrast is terrific.  A tender domestic moment is surmounted by a huge battle scene, European interlopers crushing the native Americans, of course.  In the name of flag and righteousness.  How perfect that the couple are coincidentally wearing red and blue.  These notions fill the atmosphere and float the photo into a very interesting realm.  The compositional axis of meaning flows along the upper left to lower right diagonal.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you.<br/>(An aside: Has anybody noticed an upswelling of support for returning the land to its prior, shoved-out inhabitants?  It seems history depends on where you slice it.)</td>', 'Here it''s not enough to see and feel the image, we also have to read and think it through.  The irony of contrast is terrific.  A tender domestic moment is surmounted by a huge battle scene, European interlopers crushing the native Americans, of course.  In the name of flag and righteousness.  How perfect that the couple are coincidentally wearing red and blue.  These notions fill the atmosphere and float the photo into a very interesting realm.  The compositional axis of meaning flows along the upper left to lower right diagonal.  Nice title.Thank you.(An aside: Has anybody noticed an upswelling of support for returning the land to its prior, shoved-out inhabitants?  It seems history depends on where you slice it.)', '2020-07-11 17:35:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669448, 1251372, 173844, '<td valign="top">On the get-go, this incredible blue is peacock intense, from hereon in my standrd for paradise.  Inwardly I''m vibrating, outwardly sweating cannonballs.  To reluctantly go on, the entire construction puts palaces to shame.  Oh the rust, shedding blue for a brown whose shade I can''t determine, perhaps "life-giving," sumptuous and deep as it is.  Earth and sky. Is the white an undercoat or moonlight?  Is it superficial to luxuriate and steep in such color?  Maybe, but it certainly thrills and uplifts me, invites simple exultation.  Handsomely framed on three sides by greenery.  Hang out here and forget your cares, dream anew.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'On the get-go, this incredible blue is peacock intense, from hereon in my standrd for paradise.  Inwardly I''m vibrating, outwardly sweating cannonballs.  To reluctantly go on, the entire construction puts palaces to shame.  Oh the rust, shedding blue for a brown whose shade I can''t determine, perhaps "life-giving," sumptuous and deep as it is.  Earth and sky. Is the white an undercoat or moonlight?  Is it superficial to luxuriate and steep in such color?  Maybe, but it certainly thrills and uplifts me, invites simple exultation.  Handsomely framed on three sides by greenery.  Hang out here and forget your cares, dream anew.  Nice title.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 17:58:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7669449, 1251606, 173844, '<td valign="top">Glorious.  That could be the end of it because I just want to see and see it.  But I''ll go on.  The five colored patches hang together with the satisfying precision of a jigsaw puzzle, and afford a happy sense of completion.  So the composition is unusual, a lesson in endless possibilities.  A motif throughout is the leaves, etc., floating on the water''s surface, implying star-filled heavens.  And the fish, denizens of a universe continually unfolding.  The central fish in the blue is a whisper heard on the edge of consciousness. It brings the image to the pitch of waking dreams, revelatory dreams upon which a life can be built. This photograph is wonderful.  I admire and appreciate it tremendously.  Nice title.<br/>Thank you.</td>', 'Glorious.  That could be the end of it because I just want to see and see it.  But I''ll go on.  The five colored patches hang together with the satisfying precision of a jigsaw puzzle, and afford a happy sense of completion.  So the composition is unusual, a lesson in endless possibilities.  A motif throughout is the leaves, etc., floating on the water''s surface, implying star-filled heavens.  And the fish, denizens of a universe continually unfolding.  The central fish in the blue is a whisper heard on the edge of consciousness. It brings the image to the pitch of waking dreams, revelatory dreams upon which a life can be built. This photograph is wonderful.  I admire and appreciate it tremendously.  Nice title.Thank you.', '2020-07-11 18:13:48.000000', NULL, 1),
